id: media-scrub-drag
section: Media and sound
item: The video's sliders by finger: a drag on the volume slider changes the volume and a drag of the scrubber's thumb seeks (the page reads them back); a slider is XUL scale content inside the video's anonymous controls, which the adapter's interactive-rect answer does not name, so the drag pans instead (T-598)
shells: enyo mochi mojo
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-media-test.html?src=clip60av.webm&wide=1
kit: cavekit-gre-widgets.md R1
known: T-598 never
# the page starts its clip by itself, with sound: the shipped default refuses that (T-603, off by the owner), so this test turns it on
prefs: jihad.media.autoplayWithSound=true
wait rect v 20
calibrate 'sel:#status'
wait text status playing 15
tap v
wait text status 'paused' 5
wait rect 'anon:#v|controlBar' 5
wait rect 'anon:#v|volumeControl' 5
measure 'anon:#v|volumeControl'
measure 'anon:#v|scrubber'
drag-off 'anon:#v|volumeControl' 28 12 4 12 800
wait text vol 'volume=0.' 5
# the drag starts inside the visible track (the scale's box is wider than its track: 20 px in lands left of it, on the
# gap after the play button, and nothing seeks) and ends past the track's end, where the slider clamps to the duration
drag-off 'anon:#v|scrubber' 80 10 641 10 1000
wait settled 4
wait text seek 60 4
shoot seek
